From c3639e3b45918e3ef3a78e0f3a6e3dad74805d18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: astrangedaytoday15-dev <342675337+astrangedaytoday15-dev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 05:30:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Bot Control B3: command panel

One bot command panel on the Live Map (selected bot), in World 3D
(followed bot) and in Instance Watch (selected party bot): self command
buttons, master buttons for a bot in the owner's group, strategy chips
from the live WMB1 sample (click removes, "+" adds from a short list), a
text box for one allowlisted command, and the reply line. The panel is
built once and updated in place, so redraws keep typing and open lists;
a strategy change is highlighted when the next sample shows it.

World 3D now keeps the stream's bot decisions. A "Bot commands" option
(bot-commands.json in the data dir, off by default) hides the panels and
refuses sends without a restart. WOWMIN_BOT_OWNER_ACCOUNT names the
owner's account for the master buttons. The allowlist mirror moves to
bot-command-rules.ts so the renderer shares it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
